  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Mishti doi"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is named for its character: "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "mishti doi term",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "mishti-doi-term"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " literally means sweet yoghurt. The sweetness comes from "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "jaggery term ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "jaggery-term"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", which gives a deeper colour and flavour than white sugar. The milk is first reduced by "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "reduction",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "reduction"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " to concentrate it before setting."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The milk must cool to 45C before you add the yoghurt starter. Too hot kills the culture; too cold and the yoghurt will not set."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "whole-milk",
              "amount": 1000,
              "unit": "ml",
              "prepNote": null,
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "plain-yoghurt",
              "amount": 3,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": "as the starter culture",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "jaggery",
              "amount": 80,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "grated or crushed",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            }
          ],
          "defaultServings": 4
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Pour milk into a heavy saucepan. Bring to a boil over medium heat, stirring to prevent a skin forming."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Reduce heat and simmer, stirring often, for 15 minutes until the milk reduces by about one quarter."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add grated jaggery to the hot milk. Stir until completely dissolved."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Allow the milk to cool to 45C. It should feel just warm to the touch, not hot."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Whisk the plain yoghurt until smooth. Stir into the cooled jaggery milk."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Pour into clay pots or ramekins. Cover loosely."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Leave in a warm place (around 30C) for 6-8 hours until set. Then chill for at least 2 hours before serving."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Mishti doi does not set and remains liquid",
              "cause": "Milk was too hot or too cold when the yoghurt culture was added",
              "fix": "Use a thermometer to check 43-46C before adding the starter. If it is liquid after 8 hours, the culture may be dead."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Set yoghurt is grainy and watery",
              "cause": "Jaggery was added too hot and split the milk proteins slightly",
              "fix": "Add jaggery to milk that has cooled slightly below boiling. Stir until fully dissolved before proceeding."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Mishti doi is one of the most iconic preparations of Bengal, sold in every sweet shop alongside rasgulla and sandesh. Clay pots called bhaand are the traditional vessel: the unglazed clay absorbs excess whey, helping the yoghurt set firmer and with a cleaner texture. The dish is served at weddings, festivals, and as a daily dessert. In Bogra in Bangladesh, the mishti doi has particular regional fame."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
